        "title": "Superscalar and Out-of-Order Execution",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "A pipelined in-order processor approaches 1 IPC (instruction per cycle). But stalls from hazards reduce it. Superscalar execution attacks throughput by issuing multiple instructions per cycle. Out-of-order execution attacks latency by reordering instructions to hide stalls. Modern high-performance cores combine both."
    },
